    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d189">

                <pb facs="0261" n="161" sameAs="frus:frus1920v03/pg161"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">812.00/25218a</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chief of the Division of Mexican Affairs,
                        Department of State</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Johnston</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the First Secretary of the Mexican Embassy</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Téllez</hi>)</head>
                <p>The Chief of the Division of Mexican Affairs, Department of State, presents his
                    compliments to the First Secretary of the Mexican Embassy, and has the honor to
                    inform him that the Grand Jury sitting at San Antonio, Texas, has, upon the
                    recommendation of the agents of the Department of Justice, voted conspiracy
                    indictments against the following persons, namely, General Lucio Blanco,
                    Bernardo Blanco, Marciano Gonzales, Leon Taurel, Francisco Vas-quez Gomez, Alejo
                    Gonzales, Pedro Villaseñor, Pablo Villanueva, Pedro Guzman, Antonio Maldonado,
                    and Fernando Cuen.</p>
                <p>Mr. Charles M. Johnston embraces this occasion for renewing to Señor Manuel
                    Tellez the assurances of his distinguished consideration.</p>
                <closer>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-left">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi>
                        </placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1920-12-27"><hi
                                rendition="#italic">December 27, 1920</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
